            <ArticleTitle>Reversibly Tunable White-Light Emissions of Styrylpyridiniums with Cucurbiturils in Aqueous Solution.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6650-6653</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03377</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The different excimer emissions based on a series of host-guest complexes of dipolar dyes styrylpyridiniums (An and Bn) with cucurbit[n]urils (CB[n]) are reported. The syn- and anti- excimers due to the opposite stacking orientations have been well investigated both in experiments and DFT calculations. Furthermore, reversibly color-tunable luminescent supramolecular assemblies including near white-light emission with CIE coordinates (0.32, 0.29) were achieved by competitive inclusion of An-CB[7] with ADA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
